# Kept out of version control only because CI is not enabled on main yet.
#
# 2026-11-17 correction: the "workflow scope" obstacle applies to OAuth App
# tokens ONLY. Verified on this machine:
#   git push over HTTPS  -> "refusing to allow an OAuth App to create or update
#                           workflow ... without `workflow` scope"
#   POST /git/trees      -> 404 (REST under OAuth)
#   git push over SSH    -> SUCCESS  (git@github.com:sprw-li/dsh-model-council)
# SSH keys are not OAuth Apps, so they can push workflow files. The `verify`
# workflow was accepted by GitHub and ran green on ubuntu-latest in 49s:
#   https://github.com/sprw-li/dsh-model-council/actions/runs/43903527781
#
# To enable CI (no browser authorization needed):
#   git add -f .github/workflows/verify.yml
#   git commit -m "ci: enable the verify workflow" && git push origin main
#   (then delete this .gitignore line)
# Until then `npm run verify` is the authoritative gate.
.github/workflows/
